    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">HostPapa is the right fit for small business websites, WordPress sites, and developers who want managed hosting with a real sustainability story. The carbon-neutral commitment is verifiable — they've been a recognized green host since 2007, well before "green hosting" became a marketing line. The trade-off is the $19.99/mo starting price (3x RackNerd's $1.99) and no APAC datacenters. If your audience is in North America or Europe, and you want a managed experience with cPanel + Softaculous + free migration + free CDN, HostPapa is a strong middle-tier option. If you're on a tight budget or need a Tokyo / Singapore node, look at RackNerd for the budget tier or Vultr for global reach.</p>
